1.Open Zomato.com in Chrome, press F12 to open DevTools, and use the device toolbar to simulate the site on iPhone 12, iPad, and a standard desktop. List 3 layout or UI changes you observe between these views.
Answer :

>>When Zomato.com is opened in Chrome and tested using DevTools Device Toolbar on iPhone 12, iPad, and Desktop, the following UI changes are  observed:

1)Navigation: On iPhone 12, the navigation is more compact and simplified. On iPad and Desktop, more menu options are visible.
2)Content Layout: On iPhone 12, restaurant cards and content are mostly arranged in a single-column layout. On iPad and Desktop, multiple cards can appear side-by-side.
3)Images and Spacing: On mobile, images, buttons, and spacing are smaller to fit the screen. On iPad and Desktop, they become larger with more spacing.


2.Pick any Flipkart product page and resize your browser window from desktop width down to mobile width. Note at which pixel widths (breakpoints) major layout shifts happen (e.g., menu collapses, grid changes to list). List the breakpoints and describe what changes at each.
Answer :
-Above 1024 px: Desktop layout is displayed. The header, search bar, product details, images, and navigation are arranged horizontally.
-Around 768–1024 px: The layout becomes more compact. Navigation and product information reduce in size, and some elements move to -different rows.
-Around 600–767 px: The product layout starts changing to a tablet/mobile-friendly design. Product images and details may be stacked vertically, and fewer navigation options are visible.
-Below 600 px: Mobile layout is displayed. The header becomes compact, product images and information are mainly arranged vertically, and buttons such as Buy Now and Add to Cart become easier to access on a small screen.




