5.Identify 5 responsive UI issues on any one of your favorite apps' web versions (e.g., Spotify, Instagram, Swiggy) using Chrome DevTools device simulation. For each issue, describe the problem, the device size where it appears, and suggest a possible fix.
Answer :

>>I used Spotify Web as the example and tested it using Chrome DevTools Device Simulation.

1>Navigation menu overlap
Problem: The sidebar/menu can take up too much space on smaller screens.
Device size: Mobile – 375 × 667 px
Fix: Collapse the sidebar into a hamburger/menu icon on small screens.
2>Text gets truncated
Problem: Long song or playlist names may be cut off on narrow screens.
Device size: Mobile – 360 × 800 px
Fix: Use responsive text sizing and allow text to wrap or show ellipsis properly.
3>Album images become too small
Problem: Multiple album cards in a row make the images difficult to view on mobile.
Device size: Mobile – 375 × 667 px
Fix: Reduce the number of cards per row and increase the card width.
4>Player controls become crowded
Problem: Play, pause, volume, and other controls may appear too close together on small screens.
Device size: Mobile – 390 × 844 px
Fix: Hide less-important controls and provide a simplified mobile player.
5>Horizontal scrolling/content overflow
Problem: Some sections may extend beyond the screen width, causing unwanted horizontal scrolling.
Device size: Tablet – 768 × 1024 px
Fix: Use flexible widths such as percentages or CSS Grid/Flexbox and set proper responsive breakpoints.
